  "type": "numerical",
  "level": 3,
  "question": {
    "text": "When a car is approaching the observer, the frequency of horn is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>100</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Hz</mi></math>. After passing the observer, it is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>50</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Hz</mi></math>. If the observer moves with the car, the frequency will be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mi>Hz</mi></math> where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo></math>_____ .",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "200",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Apparent frequency when source of moving towards observer,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>100</mn><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mfenced><mfrac><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced></math></p><p>Here,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo></math>frequency of observer,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo></math>speed of sound&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>=</mo></math> speed of source.</p><p>Apparent frequency when source of moving away from&nbsp;observer,&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>50</mn><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mfenced><mfrac><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced></math></p><p>From above two equations, we have&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>c</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>3</mn><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>c</mi></math></p><p>Putting the value in equation&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced></math>, we have</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>100</mn><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mfrac><mi>c</mi><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>c</mi></mrow><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>200</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Hz</mi></math></p><p>Hence,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>200</mn></math>.</p></blockquote>",
